hadiths[104]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21909","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Shurahbil, he said: I took a nuhas in al-Aswaf, then Zayd ibn Thabit took it from me and released it, and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade what is between its two lava tracts."
"21910","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license in the sale of araya to be sold by its estimate in measure."
"21911","al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am leaving among you two successors: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between heaven and earth, or between heaven and earth, and my kindred, my household, and they will never separate until they come to me at the Hawd."
"21912","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit entered upon Muawiyah and narrated a hadith to him, so he ordered a man to write it, then Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to write anything of his hadith, so he erased it."
"21913","He said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, he said: They disputed about recitation in Zuhr and Asr, so they sent to Kharijah ibn Zayd, and he said: My father said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood long in standing and moved his lips; I know that was only for recitation, so I do so."
"21914","He said: Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license in the sale of araya to be sold by its estimate, and did not give license in other than that."
"21915","He said: Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Nadr narrate from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a chamber in the mosque of mats, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in it nights until people gathered to him, then they missed his voice and thought he had slept, so some of them began to clear their throats that he might come out to them, and he said: What I have seen of your doing has not ceased with you until I feared it would be ordained upon you, and if it were ordained upon you you would not uphold it; so pray, O people, in your houses, for the best prayer of a man is in his house except the prescribed prayer."
"21916","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, and Ibn Umar said: Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license in the sale of araya by its estimate."
"21917","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit for dates, then Zayd ibn Thabit informed them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license in araya."
"21918","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then we went out to the mosque and the prayer was established. I said: How long was between them? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"21919","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, assigned umra to the heir, and he said once: He decreed with umra."
"21920","Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Do you know Syriac well, for letters come to me. He said: I said: No. He said: Then learn it. So I learned it in seventeen days."
"21921","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: May Allah forgive Rafi ibn Khadij; I, by Allah, know the hadith better than him; two men came who had fought one another, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If this is your affair then do not lease farms. He said: So Rafi heard his saying: Do not lease farms."
"21922","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Sinan Said ibn Sinan narrated to us, Wahb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn al-Daylami, he said: I met Ubayy ibn Kab and said: O Abu al-Mundhir, something of this qadar has occurred in my soul, so narrate to me something that perhaps it may leave my heart. He said: If Allah punished the people of His heavens and the people of His earth, He would punish them while He is not unjust to them, and if He had mercy on them His mercy to them would be better than their deeds, and if you spent the mountain of Uhud in gold in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in qadar and know that what befell you would never have missed you and what missed you would never have befallen you, and if you died upon other than that you would enter the Fire. He said: Then I came to Hudhayfah and he said to me the like of that, and I came to Ibn Masud and he said to me the like of that, and I came to Zayd ibn Thabit and he narrated to me from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of that."
"21923","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Umar ibn Sulayman of the offspring of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman, from his father, that Zayd ibn Thabit came out from Marwan near midday, so we said: Nothing sent to him at this hour except for something he asked him about, so I stood to him and asked him, and he said: Yes, he asked us about things I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us and memorizes it until he conveys it to another, for many a carrier of fiqh is not a faqih, and many a carrier of fiqh to one more understanding than him."
"21924","Three traits over which the heart of a Muslim never harbors ghill ever: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere counsel to rulers, and adherence to the congregation, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
"21925","And he said: Whoever has the Hereafter as his concern, Allah gathers his affair and places his richness in his heart, and the world comes to him humbled, and whoever has this world as his intention, Allah scatters his livelihood upon him and places his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of this world comes to him except what is decreed for him."
"21926","And he asked us about the middle prayer, and it is Zuhr."
"21927","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Yazid ibn Qusayt, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: I recited al-Najm to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not prostrate."
"21928","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm ibn Sukhayr, from Ubaydullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the fear prayer at Dhi Qarad, a land of the land of Banu Sulaym; the people lined behind him in two rows, a row facing the enemy and a row behind him, then he prayed with the row next to him one rakah, then these drew back to the stations of these and these to the stations of these, then he prayed with them another rakah."
"21929","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Rukayn al-Fazari, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the fear prayer and mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"21930","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Bisr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in a chamber and would come out to pray in it, and his companions noticed him and would pray with his prayer."
"21931","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Zibriqan narrate from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray Zuhr at the hajirah, and there was no prayer harder upon the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than it. He said: Then there was revealed: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer. And he said: Indeed before it are two prayers and after it are two prayers."
"21932","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Kathir ibn al-Salt, he said: Ibn al-As and Zayd ibn Thabit would write the masahif, then they passed over this verse, and Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The old man and the old woman, when they commit zina, stone them outright. Then Umar said: When this was revealed I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Write it for me. Shubah said: As if he disliked that. Then Umar said: Do you not see that the old man, if he is not muhsan, is flogged, and that the young man, if he commits zina and has been muhsan, is stoned."
"21933","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hadir ibn al-Muhajir al-Bahili, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrate from Zayd ibn Thabit that a wolf tore into a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a marwah, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license to eat it."
"21934","Abu Amir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform wudu from what fire has touched."
"21935","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Adiyy ibn Thabit informed me, Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to Uhud, then some people who had gone out with him returned, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were two parties, a party saying with killing them and a party saying no, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: What is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed it is Taybah, and it expels filth as fire expels the dross of silver."
"21936","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Kathir ibn Aflah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We were ordered to glorify at the end of every prayer thirty-three times and praise thirty-three times and magnify thirty-four times, then a man of the Ansar was visited in a dream and it was said to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered you to glorify at the end of every prayer such-and-such. The Ansari said in his dream: Yes. He said: Then make them twenty-five, twenty-five, and put tahlil among them. Then when morning came he went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then do so."
"21937","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: I would write for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Write: The sitting among the believers and the mujahidun in the way of Allah are not equal. Then Abdullah Ibn Umm Maktum came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love jihad in the way of Allah, but I have infirmity and you see, and my sight has gone. Zayd said: So the thigh of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, grew heavy upon my thigh until I feared it would crush it, then he said: Write: The sitting among the believers, other than those of harm, and the mujahidun in the way of Allah are not equal. Yaqub narrated to us."
"21938","My father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi narrated to me that he said: I saw Marwan ibn al-Hakam sitting in the mosque, so I came until I sat beside him, and he informed us that Zayd ibn Thabit informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dictated to him: The sitting are not equal. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"21939","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a night and the people of the mosque heard his prayer. He said: So the people were many the second night, and the voice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was hidden from them, so they began to seek attention and clear their throats. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked out upon them and said: You have not ceased with what you do until I feared it would be ordained upon you, and if it were ordained upon you you would not uphold it; and the best prayer of a man is in his house except the prescribed prayer."
"21940","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"21941","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, the like of it, except that he said: May Allah fight the Jews."
"21942","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Ibn Shimasah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day when he said: Tuba for Sham, Tuba for Sham. I said: What is with Sham? He said: The angels are spreading their wings over Sham."
"21943","Yahya ibn Ishaq informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah informed him that Zayd ibn Thabit said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, compiling the Quran from patches, when he said: Tuba for Sham. It was said: And why is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Indeed the angels of the Rahman are spreading their wings over it."
"21944","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah wrote to me informing me from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped in the mosque. I said to Ibn Luhayah: In the mosque of his house? He said: No, in the mosque of the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21945","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me that Zayd ibn Thabit or Abu Ayyub said to Marwan: Did I not see you shorten the two prostrations of Maghrib; I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in them al-Araf."
"21946","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked toward Yemen and said: O Allah, turn their hearts, and looked from such-and-such direction and said: O Allah, turn their hearts, and bless for us our sa and our mudd."
"21947","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Sinan narrate from Wahb ibn Khalid al-Himsi, from Ibn al-Daylami, he said: Something of qadar occurred in my soul, so I came to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: If Allah punished the people of His heavens and the people of His earth, He would punish them without being unjust to them, and if He had mercy on them His mercy to them would be better than their deeds, and if you had the mountain of Uhud, or the like of the mountain of Uhud, in gold and spent it in the way of Allah, Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in qadar and know that what befell you would never have missed you and that what missed you would never have befallen you, and that if you die upon other than this you enter the Fire."
"21948","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qabisah ibn Dhuayb say: Aishah informed the family of al-Zubayr that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with her two rakahs after Asr, and they would pray them. Qabisah said: Then Zayd ibn Thabit said: May Allah forgive Aishah; we know the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, better than Aishah; that was only because some bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at midday and sat asking him and he gave them fatwa until he prayed Zuhr and did not pray two rakahs, then he sat giving them fatwa until he prayed Asr, then he left to his house and mentioned that he had not prayed anything after Zuhr, so he prayed them after Asr. May Allah forgive Aishah; we know the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, better than Aishah; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade prayer after Asr."
"21949","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Aishah that she informed the family of al-Zubayr and mentioned its meaning."
"21950","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah."
"21951","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sell fruit until its ripeness appears."
"21952","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then we went out to the prayer. He said: I said to Zayd: How long between that? He said: As much as reciting fifty verses."
"21953","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, the orators of the Ansar stood, and some of them said: O company of Muhajirun, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he employed a man of you would join with him a man of us, so we think this affair should be undertaken by two men, one of you and the other of us. He said: Then the orators of the Ansar followed upon that. He said: Then Zayd ibn Thabit stood and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was of the Muhajirun, and the imam is only of the Muhajirun, and we are his Ansar as we were the Ansar of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then Abu Bakr stood and said: May Allah reward you with good, O company of Ansar, and confirm your speaker. Then he said: By Allah, if you did other than that we would not make peace with you."
"21954","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, that his father Zayd informed him that when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Medina, Zayd said: I was taken to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I pleased him, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a boy of Banu al-Najjar with him of what Allah revealed to you a dozen-odd surahs. That pleased the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Zayd, learn for me the book of the Jews, for I, by Allah, do not trust the Jews with my book. Zayd said: So I learned their book; fifteen nights had not passed over me until I mastered it, and I would read to him their letters when they wrote to him and answer from him when he wrote."
"21955","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came at his arrival in Medina and mentioned the like of it."
"21956","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Yazid said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Waki, al-Dastawai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and went out to the mosque and the prayer was established, so I said: How long between them? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses. He said: Yazid said in his hadith: So I said to Zayd: How long was between them? He said: About fifty verses."
"21957","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Yazid said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Waki, al-Dastawai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and went out to the mosque and the prayer was established, so I said: How long between them? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses. He said: Yazid said in his hadith: So I said to Zayd: How long was between them? He said: About fifty verses."
"21958","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Yazid said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, and Waki, al-Dastawai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and went out to the mosque and the prayer was established, so I said: How long between them? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses. He said: Yazid said in his hadith: So I said to Zayd: How long was between them? He said: About fifty verses."
"21959","Waki narrated to us, al-Dastawai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then we went out to the mosque and the prayer was established. I said: How long was between them? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"21960","Waki narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he was asked about recitation in Zuhr and Asr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would prolong the standing and move his lips."
"21961","Waki and Yazid said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: I recited to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, al-Najm and he did not prostrate in it. Yazid said: I recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21962","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best prayer of a man is in his house except the prescribed."
"21963","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, and Uthman ibn Umar, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah fight the Jews. And Uthman said: May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"21964","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he dictated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Tawus, from a man, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, assigned ruqba to the heir."
"21965","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license to the owner of the ariyyah to sell it by its estimate."
"21966","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: May Allah forgive Rafi ibn Khadij; I, by Allah, know the hadith better than him; two men came who had fought one another, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If this is your affair then do not lease farms. He said: So Rafi heard his saying: Do not lease farms."
"21967","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari al-Tai, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When this verse was revealed: When the help of Allah and the conquest comes, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited it until he completed it and said: People are one division and I and my companions are a division. And he said: There is no hijrah after the conquest, but jihad and intention. Then Marwan said to him: You have lied, and with him were Rafi ibn Khadij and Zayd ibn Thabit, sitting with him upon the bed, so Abu Said al-Khudri said: If these two wished they would narrate to you, so Marwan raised the stick to strike him, and when they saw that they said: He spoke the truth."
"21968","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Adiyy ibn Thabit informed me, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to Uhud, then some people who had gone out with him returned, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were concerning them two parties, a party saying with killing them and a party saying no. And Ibn Jafar said: The people were concerning them two parties, a party saying with killing them and a party saying no. Bahz said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: What is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed it is Taybah, and it expels filth as fire expels the dross of silver."
"21969","Affan narrated to us and said in it: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid and mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Bahz."
"21970","Kathir narrated to us, from Jafar, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us mukhabarah. I said: And what is mukhabarah? He said: Hiring the land for half or a third or a quarter."
"21971","Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, partitioned a chamber in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would come out in the night and pray in it, so they prayed with him his prayer, meaning men, and they would come to him every night until one night of the nights the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not come out to them, so they cleared their throats and raised their voices. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to them angry. He said: Then he said to them: O people, your doing has not ceased with you until I thought it would be ordained upon you, so upon you is prayer in your houses, for the best prayer of a man is in his house except the prescribed prayer."
"21972","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said to me: Did I not see you tonight lighten the recitation in the two prostrations of Maghrib; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would recite in them the longer of the two long ones."
"21973","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Adiyy ibn Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to Uhud, some people who had gone out with him returned, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were two parties, a party saying: We kill them, and a party saying: No. Ibn Jafar said: A party saying: Killing them, and a party saying: No. Bahz said: So Allah revealed: What is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed it is Taybah, and it expels filth as fire expels the dross of silver."
"21974","Fayyad ibn Muhammad Abu Muhammad al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Jafar, meaning Ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us mukhabarah. He said: And it was said to him: What is mukhabarah? He said: To take the land for half or a third or a quarter or the likes of this."
"21975","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Adiyy ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid narrating from Zayd ibn Thabit that he said concerning this verse: What is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites, and Allah cast them back for what they earned. He said: Some people of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned, and the people were concerning them two parties, a party saying: Killing them, and a party saying: No, so this verse was revealed: What is with you that you are two parties concerning the hypocrites. And he said: Indeed it is Taybah, and it expels filth as fire expels the dross of silver."
"21976","Bahz ibn Asad Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he took suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then we went out until we came to the prayer. Anas said: So I said to Zayd: How long was between that? He said: As much as reciting fifty verses or sixty verses."
"21977","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license in the sale of araya by its estimate in measure."
"21978","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Makhul and Atiyyah and Damrah and Rashid, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he was asked about a husband and a full sister, so he gave the husband half and the sister half, and he was spoken to about that, and he said: I attended the Messenger of Allah; he decreed with that."
"21979","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Kharijah ibn Zayd informed me that Zayd ibn Thabit said: When we copied the masahif, a verse of Surat al-Ahzab was missing; I had heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite it, so I sought it and did not find it with anyone except with Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, whose testimony the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made as the testimony of two men: the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Among the believers are men true to what they covenanted Allah."
"21980","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Marwan informed him that Zayd ibn Thabit said to him: Why do I see you recite in Maghrib short surahs; I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite in it the longer of the two long ones. Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: And what are the longer of the two long ones? He said: al-Araf."
"21981","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me that Kharijah ibn Zayd al-Ansari informed him that his father Zayd ibn Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Perform wudu from what fire has touched."
"21982","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Zayd informed me that he heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: A verse of Surat al-Ahzab was missing when we copied the masahif; I had heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recite it: Men true to what they covenanted Allah. So I sought it and found it with Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, and I appended it in its surah in the mushaf."
"21983","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: Abu Bakr sent to me at the killing of the people of Yamamah, and Umar was sitting with him, and Abu Bakr said: O Zayd ibn Thabit, you are a young intelligent youth we do not suspect; you used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so trace the Quran and collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain of the mountains it would not have been heavier upon me than what he ordered me of collecting the Quran. So I said: Do you do something the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not do? He said: It is, by Allah, good. So Abu Bakr kept returning to me until Allah expanded my chest with that with which He expanded the chest of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"21984","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Tawus, from a man, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, assigned ruqba to the one to whom it is given and umra to the one to whom it is given for life."
"21985","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrate, saying: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Marwan informed him, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said to me: Why do you recite in Maghrib the short Mufassal; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would recite in the Maghrib prayer the longer of the two long ones. He said: I said to Urwah: What are the longer of the two long ones? He said: al-Araf."
"21986","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: I read in the book of Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Kharijah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning wudu from what fire has touched."
"21987","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Umra is for the heir."
"21988","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Tawus informed him that Hujr al-Madari informed him that he heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Umra is in inheritance."
"21989","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not do ruqba; whoever is given ruqba takes the path of inheritance."
"21990","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Shibl, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is given an umra, it is for the one given it in his life and his death; do not do ruqba, for whoever is given ruqba anything takes the path of inheritance."
"21991","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Kharijah ibn Zayd or another, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: When the masahif were written I missed a verse I used to hear from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I found it with Khuzaymah al-Ansari: Among the believers are men true to what they covenanted Allah, to alteration. He said: Khuzaymah was called Dhu al-Shahadatayn; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, allowed his testimony as the testimony of two men. al-Zuhri said: And he was killed on the day of Siffin with Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"21992","Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Abu Sinan al-Shaybani, from Wahb al-Himsi, from Ibn al-Daylami, he said: I came to Ubayy ibn Kab and said to him: Something of qadar has occurred in my soul, so I would like you to narrate to me a hadith that perhaps Allah may remove from me what I find. He said: If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, punished the people of the heavens and the people of the earth, He would punish them while He is not unjust to them, and if He had mercy on them His mercy to them would be better than their deeds, and if Uhud were yours in gold and you spent it in the way of Allah, then you did not believe in qadar and know that what befell you would never have missed you and that what missed you would never have befallen you, nothing would be accepted from you, and if you died upon other than that you would enter the Fire. And you must meet my brother Abdullah ibn Masud and ask him. Then he met Abdullah and he said to him the like of that, then he met Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and he said to him the like of that, then he met Zayd ibn Thabit and he said to him the like of that, except that he narrated it to him from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21993","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am leaving among you two successors: the Book of Allah and my household, and they will never separate until they come to me at the Hawd together."
"21994","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform wudu from what fire has touched."
"21995","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Nafi ibn Umar, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave license in the ariyyah to be taken for the like of its estimate in dates; its people eat it fresh."
"21996","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah, except that he gave license to the people of araya to sell it for the like of its estimate."
"21997","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Masud al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a wall of the walls of Medina in which were graves, and he was upon his mule, so it shied with him and almost cast him. Then he said: Who knows the occupants of these graves? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, people who perished in Jahiliyyah. Then he said: Were it not that you would not bury, I would supplicate Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to let you hear the torment of the grave. Then he said to us: Seek refuge with Allah from the torment of Hell. We said: We seek refuge with Allah from the torment of Hell. Then he said: Seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal. So we said: We seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal. Then he said: Seek refuge with Allah from the torment of the grave. So we said: We seek refuge with Allah from the torment of the grave. Then he said: Seek refuge with Allah from the trial of life and death. We said: We seek refuge with Allah from the trial of life and death."
"21998","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Kathir ibn Aflah, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: We were ordered to glorify at the end of every prayer thirty-three tasbihahs and praise thirty-three tahmidahs and magnify thirty-four takbirahs. He said: Then a man saw in a dream and said: You were ordered with thirty-three tasbihahs and thirty-three tahmidahs and thirty-four takbirahs, so if you put tahlil among them and made them twenty-five. So I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: You have seen, so do so, or the like of that."
"21999","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform wudu from what fire has touched."
"22000","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade praying when the horn of the sun rises or its horn sets, and said: It rises between the two horns of Satan, or from between the two horns of Satan."
"22001","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharija ibn Zayd, he said, Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah while we were trading in fruits before their ripeness had appeared, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a dispute, so he said: What is this, and it was said to him: These bought fruits, saying: We were struck by dumman and qusham, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not trade in them until their ripeness appears."
"22002","Surayj narrated to us, and he said: al-udman and al-qusham."
"22003","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Sad al-Khurasani narrated to me, he heard Shurahbil ibn Sad saying: Zayd ibn Thabit came to us while we were in a garden of ours, and with us were traps we were setting, so he shouted at us and drove us away, and said: Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade its hunting."
"22004","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Abi al-Zinad, from Kharija ibn Zayd, he said, Zayd ibn Thabit said: I was sitting beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day when revelation was sent down to him, he said, and tranquility overcame him, and his thigh fell upon my thigh when the tranquility overcame him, Zayd said: By Allah I never found anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then it was lifted from him, and he said: Write O Zayd, so I took a shoulder blade, and he said: Write: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and the mujahidin, the whole verse, up to His saying: a great reward, so I wrote that on a shoulder blade, then Ibn Umm Maktum stood when he heard it, and he was a blind man, so he stood when he heard the virtue of the mujahidin, he said: O Messenger of Allah, then what of one who cannot perform jihad among those who are blind and the like of that, Zayd said: By Allah his speech had not passed, or it was only that he finished his speech, when tranquility overcame the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his thigh fell upon my thigh, and I felt of its weight as I had felt the first time, then it was lifted from him, and he said: Read, so I read to him: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and the mujahidin, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except those with disability, Zayd said: So I appended it, and by Allah it is as if I am looking at its addition at a crack that was in the shoulder blade."
"22005","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from his father, from Kharija ibn Zayd, he said, Zayd ibn Thabit said: Allah Almighty sent down to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was beside him, then he mentioned the like of it."
"22006","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Damra ibn Habib ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Abi al-Darda, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him a supplication and commanded him to maintain it with his family every day, he said: Say every day when you enter the morning: At Your service O Allah at Your service, and at Your aid, and good is in Your Hands, and from You, and by You, and to You, O Allah whatever saying I said, or vow I vowed, or oath I swore, then Your will is before it, what You willed was, and what You did not will was not, and there is no power nor strength except by You, indeed You are over all things Capable, O Allah whatever prayer I prayed then upon whom You prayed, and whatever curse I cursed then upon whom You cursed, indeed You are my Guardian in this world and the Hereafter, cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous, I ask You O Allah for contentment after decree, and coolness of life after death, and delight of looking at Your Face, and longing to meet You, without harmful adversity nor misleading trial, I seek refuge in You O Allah from wronging, or being wronged, or transgressing, or being transgressed against, or acquiring a nullifying sin, or a sin not forgiven, O Allah Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Possessor of majesty and honor, for I covenant to You in this worldly life, and I call You to witness, and sufficient are You as Witness, that I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, no partner for You, to You is dominion and to You is praise, and You are over all things Capable, and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger, and I bear witness that Your promise is true, and meeting You is true, and Paradise is true, and the Hour is coming, no doubt in it, and You will resurrect those in the graves, and I bear witness that if You entrust me to myself You entrust me to waste, and exposure, and sin, and error, and I trust only in Your mercy, so forgive me all my sin, indeed none forgives sins but You, and turn to me in forgiveness, indeed You are the Oft-Returning the Merciful."
"22007","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Kharija ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought at his arrival in Madinah, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Sulayman ibn Dawud, from Abi al-Zinad, from his father, from Kharija ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit."
"22008","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abu al-Zinad narrated to me, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: A man from the people of Syria came with oil, so I bargained with him among the merchants who bargained, until I bought it from him, he said, then a man stood toward me and offered me profit in it until he satisfied me, he said: So I took his hand to strike upon it, then a man took my arm from behind me, so I turned to him, and behold it was Zayd ibn Thabit, and he said: Do not sell it where you bought it until you move it to your saddlebag, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, so I withheld my hand."
"22009","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, that Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed him, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"22010","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me in the markets, and with me was a bird I had hunted, he said: So he slapped the back of my neck and released it from my hand, and said: Did you not know O enemy of yourself that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade what is between its two lava plains."
"22011","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: I passed by the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was taking suhur eating dates, so he said: Come and eat, so I said: I intend fasting, so he said: And I intend what you intend, so we ate, then we stood for prayer, and between our eating and our standing for prayer was the measure of what a man recites fifty verses."
"22012","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No fruit is sold for dates, and no fruit is sold until its ripeness appears, he said: Then Zayd ibn Thabit met Abdullah ibn Umar and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted araya, Sufyan said: Araya were palms that were gifted to the poor, so they could not wait with them, and would sell them for whatever fruit they wished."
